{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789236204,"nonce":"kHyz3RASMTAN0au5D83b9lrSiEM=","title":"Interpreter looks up the frame's module by name on every call and return","message":"Profile of bench/delta_blue.wren in --mode interpreter (macOS sample, 3 s): 25-30% of samples in SipHash + memcmp under run_fiber_loop. The fiber loop re-resolves vm.engine.modules.get_mut(module_name) at the top of every iteration, i.e. on every call, return and fiber switch, hashing the module name string each time. Fix: cache the entry pointer keyed by the Rc pointer of the frame's module name plus the module count (a new module can rehash the table). delta_blue interpreter 640 -\u003e 450 ms, tiered wall 142 -\u003e 124 ms (wren_cli 100 ms).\n\nNext per-call costs in the profile, unaddressed: thread-local access for the live-register guard and JIT context (7%), ensure_bytecode per call (3%), register-file UNDEF fill, MirCallFrame push/drop.","files":null}]}